bid:8facb614-80ac-4873-8619-b37c2ad0ed62 a bbqs:Project ;
    bbqs:abstract """Project Summary/Abstract
Post-traumatic stress disorder (PTSD) is marked by emotional dysregulation, hyperarousal, and intrusive
autobiographical memories, yet current tools lack the ability to objectively monitor these symptoms in real time,
especially outside clinical settings. This project will develop a self-powered smart contact lens (SCL) platform
that integrates high-speed pupillometry with battery-free biosensing of tear film neurochemicals including cortisol,
serotonin, and neuropeptide Y to assess emotional and autonomic states during naturalistic experiences. The
lens will communicate wirelessly with custom smart glasses that power the system, record synchronized audio
and video, and trigger intracranial EEG (iEEG) recordings via a wearable electromagnet cap. We will deploy the
system in ambulatory participants with existing iEEG recording devices implanted in the amygdala and
hippocampus, both in lab and at home, to characterize the correspondence between peripheral biosignals and
neural activity during emotionally salient experiences. By enabling mobile, multimodal tracking of emotional
arousal and stress in real-world contexts, this platform offers transformative potential for understanding and
treating PTSD and related affective disorders.""" ;
    bbqs:award_amount 1368212 ;
    bbqs:description """Project Summary/Abstract
Post-traumatic stress disorder (PTSD) is marked by emotional dysregulation, hyperarousal, and intrusive
autobiographical memories, yet current tools lack the ability to objectively monitor these symptoms in real time,
especially outside clinical settings. This project will develop a self-powered smart contact lens (SCL) platform
that integrates high-speed pupillometry with battery-free biosensing of tear film neurochemicals including cortisol,
serotonin, and neuropeptide Y to assess emotional and autonomic states during naturalistic experiences. The
lens will communicate wirelessly with custom smart glasses that power the system, record synchronized audio
and video, and trigger intracranial EEG (iEEG) recordings via a wearable electromagnet cap. We will deploy the
system in ambulatory participants with existing iEEG recording devices implanted in the amygdala and
hippocampus, both in lab and at home, to characterize the correspondence between peripheral biosignals and
neural activity during emotionally salient experiences. By enabling mobile, multimodal tracking of emotional
arousal and stress in real-world contexts, this platform offers transformative potential for understanding and
treating PTSD and related affective disorders.""" ;
    bbqs:fiscal_year 2026 ;
    bbqs:grant_number "U01MH143789" ;
    bbqs:mechanism "U01" ;
    bbqs:name "A smart lens platform for real-world event capture and synchronized deep brain dynamics" ;
    bbqs:onboarding_status "not_started" ;
    bbqs:reporter_project_num "1U01MH143789-01" ;
    bbqs:studies_human true ;
    bbqs:title "A smart lens platform for real-world event capture and synchronized deep brain dynamics" .

